  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "Fixes disposal throwing when the JavaScript side has already gone. DisposeAsync guarded its teardown with a single catch for JSDisconnectedException, which only a Blazor Server circuit ever raises; every other host reaches the same state by another route, and when the JS side goes first - a WebView reload, a WKWebView content process restart, the renderer being disposed at shutdown - the module's entry is gone from the interop registry and the call arrives back as a plain JSException. That escaped disposal and resurfaced later as an unobserved task exception naming a component that was already gone, and it skipped the DotNetObjectReference release, pinning the instance it was meant to free. Both exceptions are now handled, the module reference is released even when destroy itself fails, and a second disposal is a no-op. Affects MAUI BlazorWebView and WASM hosts in particular. Same vendored Swiper 14.0.6 bundle.",
